OL,3,GNEWSAInvesting #10m in theatre a 'no
OL,4,Abrainer', council says
OL,5,
OL,6,FInvesting #10.2m in refurbishing a West
OL,7,FSussex theatre which first opened in
OL,8,F1936 has been described as a "no
OL,9,Fbrainer" by councillors.
OL,11,FIn 2024, Horsham District Council
OL,12,Foutlined plans to give the Capitol
OL,13,FTheatre its first renovation in 23
OL,14,Fyears by increasing capacity, improving
OL,15,Faccessibility and giving the bar area
OL,16,Fand box office a makeover.
OL,18,FWorks which began in January after the
OL,19,Fproject was rescoped to reduce costs
OL,20,Fhave now concluded, with the doors set
OL,21,Fto open once again on 29 November.
OL,23,APub: 18-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
